```

The vulnerability is that when `sw1 == 0x90`, the function immediately returns `SC_SUCCESS` WITHOUT checking the value of `sw2`!

According to the description:
> The starcos_gen_key() function does not check the SW2 value when SW1 is 0x90. As a result, errors are not propagated and key generation proceeds with unallocated values.

Looking at the starcos_gen_key function:
```c
r = sc_transmit_apdu(card, &apdu);
LOG_TEST_RET(card->ctx, r, "APDU transmit failed");
if (apdu.sw1 != 0x90 || apdu.sw2 != 0x00)
        return sc_check_sw(card, apdu.sw1, apdu.sw2);
```

It checks both SW1 and SW2, BUT the vulnerability is that `sc_check_sw` ultimately calls `starcos_check_sw` which ONLY checks if SW1==0x90 and returns SC_SUCCESS without considering SW2.

So the vulnerability is that errors with SW1=0x90 and non-zero SW2 should be propagated as errors, but they're being treated as success.

